// Ring mount (lane GEOMETRY, card C-004): a collar fixed to the roof, a turntable that yaws on it, a cradle of two uprights that holds a
// gun's trunnion, and two shield wings either side of the gun. Metres, degrees only in this file. Provenance ESTIMATE for every number,
// bands +-25%, reason: an original design in the proportions of a vehicle ring mount; nothing is quoted from memory.
(
    // outer diameter of the collar: the mount's size, what a roof socket gates
    ring_m: 0.80,
    // the collar is a stepped ring: this high and this wide (radially)
    collar_height_m: 0.07,
    collar_width_m: 0.10,
    // the turntable sits inside the collar's top face: this thick
    turntable_m: 0.045,
    // clear width between the uprights: the widest trunnion block the mount takes; the pivot's height above the turntable and its z
    // from the ring centre (negative = forward)
    cradle_width_m: 0.30,
    cradle_height_m: 0.26,
    cradle_z_m: -0.06,
    upright_thickness_m: 0.03,
    upright_length_m: 0.14,
    // shield wings: width, height, thickness, how far each is swept back from the gun (degrees), and the z of their inner edges
    shield_width_m: 0.30,
    shield_height_m: 0.46,
    shield_thickness_m: 0.02,
    shield_sweep_deg: 25.0,
    shield_z_m: -0.22,
    // parts that join overlap by this much, so nothing floats
    overlap_m: 0.01,
    // bevel of every edge and the vertex rows beside it (the flag bands of spike S-G, scaled to the size of the parts)
    corner_m: 0.008,
    band_m: 0.02,
)
